DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't trade the Nvidia headline.</b> The board's probe into Jensen Huang's ties to an alleged Chinese spy is a fresh hit to the biggest AI stock after a fourth straight losing week (23 highs vs 127 lows); let the US open and any company update settle first.",
"<b>Keep investing regularly, not all at once.</b> Extreme fear (Fear & Greed 22) and a VIX near 26 are when dollar-cost averaging into broad funds works better than guessing the bottom.",
"<b>Jobs raised the rate bar again.</b> NFP +165k lifted December hike odds to about 77%; avoid new high-interest debt and keep some cash/short bonds until CPI (10 Nov) and the 9 Dec Fed.",
"<b>Spread your risk beyond tech.</b> Thursday's selloff and Friday's bounce were both concentrated in chips and AI infrastructure; a broad or equal-weight fund keeps you from leaning too hard on one theme.",
"<b>Fuel is still two-sided.</b> Brent finished the week >16% lower on diplomacy hopes but settled near $98; budget for another spike if Rapidan's ~80% resume-fighting call proves right.",
"<b>Gold is still a useful small hedge.</b> Near $4,080 after giving back Thursday's spike; if you hold some, keep it a small slice.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> BTC is flat near $75.9k with ETF outflows still running; don't keep more on an exchange than you need.",
"<b>Thai investors: patient after the −2.2% SET drop.</b> October inflation jumped to 3.90%, so the BoT is unlikely to cut soon. Foreigners sold ฿4.8B, electronics (DELTA, KCE) led, and KS sees support at 1,445/1,430 this week. In our dividend table, SPALI, ICHI, PTTEP, AP, TVO and PTT still trade at or below their buy zones (green) — check payout safety first.",
"<b>Oil is calmer than the headlines.</b> Brent slipped to ~$97.7 at the open after Trump called new strikes 'highly unlikely', despite tanker fires in Hormuz; Tuesday's CPI still decides the December hike, so don't trade the first hour on headlines alone."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 22 = Extreme Fear, flat vs Thursday's close reading and down from about 26 a week ago. Momentum, put/call, VIX and safe-haven demand stayed in extreme fear after the AI week."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~44 = Elevated (flat): Saudi missile intercepts and Hormuz tanker fires offset Trump calling new Iran strikes 'highly unlikely' and Europe joining the Abu Dhabi talks."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 8 = extreme fear: Friday's small bounce did not repair Thursday's 4.4% crash below trend."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 42 = fear (23 NYSE highs vs 127 lows Friday)."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 45.4 = neutral on CNN's component; the session was a partial tech bounce inside a weak week."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 13.4 = extreme fear: protection demand remains elevated after the AI wipeout."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. Reading 9.15 = extreme fear: the VIX closed 25.64 Friday, down from 28.18 Thursday but still elevated."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 1 = extreme fear: bonds still beat stocks over the recent window despite Friday's equity bounce."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 35.6 = fear: junk demand remains soft."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 60 (flat): Trump talked down new strikes but Iran threatened 'hell' if attacked. Iran isn't a confirmed nuclear state."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 39 (from 40): Europe joins Tuesday's Abu Dhabi talks with Russia's upgraded team."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 74 (from 72): Saudi missile intercepts, Aramco building hit in Riyadh, tanker fires in Hormuz."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 13: Qatar's inspections plan, a US-China message to Tehran and confirmed Ukraine talks."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 30 (from 25): no explicit nuclear threats, but Iran scrapped its missile-range cap."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,377 Friday (+0.31%), still ~−2.7% on the week."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. −0.46% Friday to about 51,286."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. +1.09% Friday to about 24,579 after Thursday's confirmed correction; still ~−3.4% on the week."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.86% Friday, up about 2bp as jobs firmed hike odds."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$90.5 (−0.4%) early Monday after Trump called new Iran strikes 'highly unlikely'; Friday settle $90.83."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$97.7 (−0.6%) early Monday; Hormuz is still constrained, with three tanker fires reported Sunday."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$6.23/gal (AAA, 6 Nov), edging down and below the 22 Sep record of $6.53."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$4,060 spot early Monday (−0.2%); $4,000 is support."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$75.7k = bearish: a third flat day after the 5–6 Nov drop; $75k is support."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00%, held on 28 Oct with two officials wanting a hike; next decision 9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. 3.7% YoY is well above the Fed's 2% goal; the Fed's preferred PCE gauge was 3.6% in September. October CPI is due Tue 10 Nov with no YoY figures (October 2025 data gap); Wells Fargo expects +0.28% headline / +0.21% core MoM."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. +6.3% in a year, the biggest since 2022."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). About 77% for a quarter-point hike on 9 Dec as of 6 Nov after the jobs print."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. Last noted about 101.8 (2 Nov); the Bloomberg dollar gauge rose 0.3% Tuesday on strong jobs data."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~158.7 = a weak yen; the BOJ held at 1.25% but said its 2% inflation goal is met, which points to more hikes."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) and Meta's hit a record in October as AI spending strained cash flow."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct in a unanimous vote (fourth hold in a row); the BoT raised its 2026 growth forecast to 2.4%, sees inflation at 2.1% and is watching oil and El Niño risks."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,465.70 Fri 6 Nov (−2.16%), reopening Mon 9 Nov; KS sees support at 1,445/1,430 and resistance at 1,490/1,500 for 9-13 Nov."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. −฿4,794.84M on 6 Nov; local institutions −฿824M, Thai retail +฿5,597M (SET)."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};
